# Network shares to mount under /media at boot, read by
# /etc/init.d/S45shares. One share per line:
#
#     <type> <source> <name> [extra mount options]
#
#   type    cifs or nfs4
#   source  cifs: //<ip>/<share>[/<subdirectory>]
#           nfs4: <ip>:/<export>
#   name    the directory under /media to mount it at
#
# /media is MPD's music_directory, so a share mounted here shows up as a
# top-level folder in myMPD with no further configuration.
#
# Everything is mounted read-only. This is a music player.
#
# Use an IP address, not a hostname. The kernel has no resolver of its
# own, and the upcall CONFIG_DNS_RESOLVER provides needs a userspace
# helper this image does not ship.
#
# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Do NOT put a username or password on the lines below, and do not put
# them in this file: it lives in the image, which lives in git.
#
# Put them on the data partition instead, in /data/shares/<name>.cred,
# which survives a reflash:
#
#     username=someone
#     password=something
#     domain=optional
#
# chmod 600 it. /data/shares is created by S03data with mode 0700.
#
# Note that "credentials=" as a mount option does not work here. The
# kernel maps it, and "cred=", to Opt_ignore - they are meant to be
# consumed by the mount.cifs helper, which this image does not ship - so
# it would be silently discarded and the mount would fail as anonymous.
# S45shares reads the file itself and builds user=/pass= from it.
#
# A password containing a comma cannot be passed this way either, because
# the mount option string has no escaping. Change the password.
#
# With no credentials file the share is tried anonymously, which is what
# a guest-readable share wants.
#
# --- Dialect -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The kernel negotiates SMB3.1.1 down to 2.1 by default, which is what
# any NAS made this decade speaks. A server that only does SMB1 needs
# "vers=1.0" as an extra option on its line; the kernel will accept that,
# because CONFIG_CIFS_ALLOW_INSECURE_LEGACY is "default y" upstream and
# so is compiled in whether we ask for it or not.

# Site-specific. Change the address and path to your own NAS, or comment
# it out if you have none.
cifs //192.168.0.196/Tiny/MEDIA/MUSIC_DROP/Subsonic subsonic
